    <subsection xml:id="ch-10-homework-part-5">
      <title>Part 5: Contextual Analysis</title>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>
      </paragraphs>
      <p>Read the passage below and answer the questions.</p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Passage</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><foreign>Maria moved to Boston in 2018. She has lived there ever since. When I visited her last summer, she was working on her dissertation. She has been writing it for two years now. By next June, she will have finished the entire project. After that, she will be looking for a teaching position.</foreign></p>

      <paragraphs>
        <title>Exercises</title>
      </paragraphs>

      <p><em>Exercise 21.</em> Identify the tense-aspect of each verb phrase in the passage:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><p><foreign>moved</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>has lived</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>visited</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>was working</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>has been writing</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>will have finished</foreign>:</p></li>
        <li><p><foreign>will be looking</foreign>:</p></li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>Exercise 22.</em> The passage uses both <foreign>moved</foreign> (past simple) and <foreign>has lived</foreign> (present perfect). Both refer to events that began in 2018. Explain why the writer chose different tense-aspects for these two verbs.</p>



